<title>UK: World drug sales advanced 7.0 pct in Jan-Oct - IMS.</title>
<headline>World drug sales advanced 7.0 pct in Jan-Oct - IMS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceutical sales in 10 of the world's top markets rose seven percent year-on-year in local currency terms in January to October, market researcher IMS International said on Monday.</p>
<p>IMS detailed retail pharmacy sales as follows, in billion dollars. Growth rates in local currency terms -</p>
<p>		     Jan-Oct 96     Jan-Oct 95     Percent growth</p>
<p> U.S.		  48.144	    44.674	     8.0</p>
<p> Canada		 3.084	     2.962	     4.0</p>
<p> Germany	     14.030	    13.656	     8.0</p>
<p> France		12.248	    12.334	     1.0</p>
<p> Italy		  7.524	     6.305	    13.0</p>
<p> UK		     5.559	     5.169	    11.0</p>
<p> Spain		  4.287	     3.936	    10.0</p>
<p> Netherlands	  1.652	     1.719	     1.0</p>
<p> Belgium		1.666	     1.639	     7.0</p>
<p> Japan		 19.164	     21.936	    3.0</p>
<p> Selected world   117.358	    114.330	    7.0</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
